here’s no one to click the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dialog."}]},{"text":"The first build is slow","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-first-build-is-slow"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux depends on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift-syntax"},{"type":"text","text":", which the macro system compiles from source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on first build (a few minutes on CI-class hardware). It’s cached afterwards;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing is wrong. CI pipelines benefit from caching "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".build\/"},{"type":"text","text":" or DerivedData."}]},{"text":"Console shows “Re-entrant Store.send(…) — deferring”","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Console-shows-Re-entrant-Storesend-deferring"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Something called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" synchronously from inside a reducer or plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hook — usually a plugin observing state and dispatching in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":" setter fired during view updates. The store defers the inner action"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and runs it as a full cycle right after the current one, so state stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consistent — but the fault log is telling you the design wants that follow-up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dispatched from an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"text":"`call to main actor-isolated initializer … in a synchronous nonisolated context`","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"call-to-main-actor-isolated-initializer--in-a-synchronous-nonisolated-context"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is compiling in Swift 5 language mode with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux nonisolated struct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only gets a nonisolated synthesized memberwise initializer under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift 6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mode","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0"},{"type":"text","text":"); under Swift 5 mode the macro’s state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction can’t call it, and adding an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nonisolated init"},{"type":"text","text":" does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not rescue it. Switch the target to Swift 6 mode."}]},{"text":"Error: “stored properties need an explicit type annotation”","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Error-stored-properties-need-an-explicit-type-annotation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"var flag = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the compiler an inferred type, but macros can’t see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it — before this diagnostic existed, such a property was silently skipped and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its value reset on every dispatch. Write ","type":"text"},{"code":"var flag: Bool = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applies to combined declarations: split ","type":"text"},{"code":"var a, b: Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" into separate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declarations."}]},{"text":"Keychain writes fail with OSStatus −34018 (`errSecMissingEntitlement`)","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Keychain-writes-fail-with-OSStatus-%E2%88%9234018-errSecMissingEntitlement"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An unsigned local or CI build is using "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" without a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provisioning profile. This is a signing condition, not a prompt or a bug — the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data-protection keychain never prompts. Ship provisioning-profile-signed builds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"accessGroup: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; for unsigned local\/CI builds add a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"team-prefixed ","type":"text"},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entitlement. Details in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Contributors: the lint plugin doesn’t run \/ dev tooling is missing","anchor":"Contributors-the-lint-plugin-doesnt-run--dev-tooling-is-missing","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dev tooling (the Persnoop linter, the DocC plugin) is gated behind a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gitignored ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dev-tooling"},{"text":" sentinel file so it never leaks into consumers’","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependency graphs. Create it at the package root — and if the package was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"already built without it, run ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift package purge-cache"},{"text":" so SwiftPM re-reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the manifest. See the repository’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CONTRIBUTING.md","type":"codeVoice"}